## 📌 Overview

A lightweight content and enquiry management API for the Team Oreo website rebuild.

It powers admin authentication, blog publishing and (next) contact enquiries — intentionally not a CRM, enterprise CMS or multi-role platform.

### Milestone Scope & Status

| Milestone | Scope | Status |
|---|---|---|
| M1 — Contract & setup | Express app, Atlas connection, env contract | ✅ Done |
| M2 — Security & models | Admin seed / login / logout / me, auth middleware, error handling | ✅ Done |
| M3 — Blog API | Blog CRUD, slugs, drafts/publish, image uploads, validation | ✅ Done |
| M4 — Contact & dashboard | Public contact form API, admin enquiries, dashboard summary | 🔜 Next |
| M5 — Admin UI & integration | Next.js `/admin` routes, end-to-end QA | ⏳ Pending |

---

## ✨ Features

### 🔐 Authentication & Access Control

- Login / logout / session check via short-lived JWT in an HttpOnly cookie.
- Admins provisioned through a documented CLI script — no public sign-up, ever.
- Server-side `requireAdmin` middleware on every protected endpoint (hiding buttons ≠ access control).
- Login rate-limiting and deliberately generic credential errors.

### 📰 Blog Content Management

- Full CRUD with draft → publish → unpublish workflow.
- Auto-generated URL slugs with collision handling (`title`, `title-2`, `title-3`…).
- Drafts never appear in public endpoints — filtered server-side.
- Featured image uploads to Cloudinary (MIME whitelist, 5 MB cap).
- Rich-text HTML sanitized server-side before storage (stored-XSS defense).

### ✅ Quality & Reliability

- Field-level request validation with structured error responses.
- One consistent response envelope across every endpoint.
- Centralized error handler — no stack traces, credentials or DB internals ever reach clients.

---

## 🧱 Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Runtime | Node.js 20+ (ESM) · `node --watch` in dev |
| Framework | Express 4 |
| Database | MongoDB Atlas + Mongoose |
| Auth | `jsonwebtoken` + Argon2id (legacy bcrypt hashes upgraded on login), HttpOnly cookies |
| Validation | `express-validator` · `sanitize-html` |
| Uploads | `multer` → Cloudinary |
| Hardening | `helmet` · `cors` · `express-rate-limit` · `cookie-parser` |

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```text
src/
├── server.js                    # Entry point: env check → DB connect → listen
├── app.js                       # Middleware stack, route mounting, error handler
├── config/
│   └── db.js                    # Mongoose connection
├── models/
│   ├── Admin.js                 # Admin accounts
│   └── Blog.js                  # Articles + uniqueSlug() helper
├── controllers/
│   ├── authController.js        # Login / me / logout
│   ├── blogController.js       # Public + admin blog CRUD
│   └── uploadController.js     # Multer → Cloudinary
├── routes/
│   ├── authRoutes.js           # /api/admin/auth/*
│   ├── blogPublicRoutes.js     # /api/blogs/**
│   ├── blogAdminRoutes.js      # /api/admin/blogs/** (protected)
│   └── uploadRoutes.js         # /api/admin/uploads (protected)
├── middleware/
│   ├── requireAdmin.js         # Verifies cookie, loads admin, attaches req.admin
│   ├── validate.js             # express-validator results → 400 envelope
│   ├── originCheck.js          # CSRF defense: origin allowlist
│   └── rateLimiters.js         # Login limiter
└── scripts/
    └── createAdmin.js          # CLI: create/reset the first admin
```

