## ⚙️ Setup

### Prerequisites

| Tool | Why | Get it |
|---|---|---|
| Node.js ≥ 20 | Run the server | [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/) |
| MongoDB Atlas account | Free M0 cluster = your database | [mongodb.com/atlas](https://www.mongodb.com/atlas) |
| Cloudinary account | Blog image storage (optional for CRUD testing) | [cloudinary.com](https://cloudinary.com/) |

### 1️⃣ Install

```bash
git clone <repo-url>
cd <repo>
npm install
```

### 2️⃣ Configure Environment

Copy `.env.example` → `.env` and fill in real values:

```dotenv
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<pass>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/team-oreo
JWT_SECRET=<long-random-string>
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=2h
CLIENT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
```

Generate a strong JWT secret:

```bash
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
```

> ⚠️ The server refuses to start if `MONGODB_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`, or `CLIENT_ORIGIN` is missing — intentional (brief §9.2). Real secrets live only in `.env` (gitignored); `.env.example` ships blank placeholders.

#### Environment Variables

| Variable | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` | — | API port (default 5000) |
| `NODE_ENV` | — | Production enables Secure cookies (HTTPS required) |
| `MONGODB_URI` | ✅ | Atlas connection string |
| `JWT_SECRET` | ✅ | Signs session tokens |
| `JWT_EXPIRES_IN` | — | Session lifetime (default 2h) |
| `CLIENT_ORIGIN` | ✅ | Comma-separated allowlist for CORS + origin checks |
| `CLOUDINARY_*` | For uploads | Image storage credentials |

### 3️⃣ Create the First Administrator

No public sign-up exists (brief §4.2). Provision via CLI:

```bash
node src/scripts/createAdmin.js admin@teamoreo.test "StrongPassword123" "Oreo Admin"
```

Expected output:

```text
✅ Admin created: admin@teamoreo.test
```

Running it again with an existing email resets that admin's password.

### 4️⃣ Run

```bash
npm run dev   # Development — auto-restarts on file change
npm start     # Production
```

**Health check:**

`GET http://localhost:5000/api/health`

Expected response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "TeamOreo API is running"
}
```

