## 🔗 Integration Contract — Frontend, Read This

Agreed up front per brief §3.2, so parallel frontend work is safe.

| Item | Decision |
|---|---|
| API base URL (dev) | `http://localhost:5000` |
| Auth | JWT in cookie `admin_token` — HttpOnly · SameSite=Lax · Secure in prod · 2h expiry |
| Cookies on frontend | Nothing to do — same-origin requests attach it automatically |
| Recommended proxy | Next.js rewrite (below) keeps frontend + API same-origin |
| Success envelope | `{ "success": true, "data": …, "message": "…" }` |
| Error envelope | `{ "success": false, "error": { "code", "message", "fields"? } }` |
| Error codes | `VALIDATION_ERROR` · `INVALID_JSON` · `INVALID_CREDENTIALS` · `UNAUTHENTICATED` · `FORBIDDEN` · `NOT_FOUND` · `CONFLICT` · `INVALID_FILE` · `FILE_TOO_LARGE` · `RATE_LIMITED` · `INTERNAL_ERROR` |
| Status codes | 200/201 ok · 400 bad input/JSON · 401 unauthenticated · 403 bad origin · 404 missing · 409 duplicate · 413 oversized upload · 429 rate-limited · 500 internal |
| Field naming | camelCase, exactly as in the schema tables |

### Next.js Rewrite

```javascript
// next.config.js — same-origin cookie handling
async rewrites() {
  return [
    {
      source: '/api/:path*',
      destination: 'http://localhost:5000/api/:path*',
    },
  ];
}
```

---

## 📡 API Reference

**Method legend:** 🟢 GET · 🔵 POST · 🟡 PATCH · 🔴 DELETE

All admin routes require the `admin_token` cookie; requests without it get `401` before any handler runs.

### 🛡️ Authentication — `/api/admin/auth`

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| 🔵 POST | `/api/admin/auth/login` | Public | Validate credentials, set session cookie |
| 🟢 GET | `/api/admin/auth/me` | Admin | Current admin profile (password hash never returned) |
| 🔵 POST | `/api/admin/auth/logout` | Admin | Clear the session cookie |

**Login request:**

```json
{
  "email": "admin@teamoreo.test",
  "password": "StrongPassword123"
}
```

**Expected response — `200`:**

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "_id": "…",
    "email": "…",
    "name": "Oreo Admin"
  },
  "message": "Logged in"
}
```

- ❌ Wrong credentials → `401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS` — `"Invalid email or password"`, always generic.
- 🚦 Rate limit: 10 attempts / 15 min → `429`.
- 🍪 Success sets `admin_token`; no extra headers needed on later calls.

### 📰 Blog — Public (No Auth)

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| 🟢 GET | `/api/blogs` | Published only. Query: `page` · `limit` (≤50) · `category` · `search` |
| 🟢 GET | `/api/blogs/:slug` | One published article by slug — 404 for drafts/missing |

**Example request:**

```http
GET /api/blogs?page=1&limit=9&search=championship
```

**Example response:**

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "items": [
      {
        "title": "Team Oreo Wins the Championship",
        "slug": "team-oreo-wins-the-championship",
        "excerpt": "A recap of the biggest match.",
        "featuredImage": {
          "url": "https://…",
          "publicId": "…",
          "alt": "…"
        },
        "category": "News",
        "author": "Oreo Admin",
        "publishedAt": "2025-01-15T10:00:00.000Z"
      }
    ],
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 9,
    "total": 1,
    "totalPages": 1
  }
}
```

Listing responses exclude `content` (cards don't need the body — fetch it via the slug endpoint). Newest-first by `publishedAt`; search is case-insensitive across title + excerpt.

### ✏️ Blog — Admin (Session Required)

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| 🟢 GET | `/api/admin/blogs` | All statuses · query: `page` · `limit` · `status` · `category` · `search` |
| 🟢 GET | `/api/admin/blogs/:id` | Full article including content (edit form) |
| 🔵 POST | `/api/admin/blogs` | Create draft or published article |
| 🟡 PATCH | `/api/admin/blogs/:id` | Partial update — any subset of fields, including status |
| 🔴 DELETE | `/api/admin/blogs/:id` | Hard delete — confirm in the UI |

**Create blog request** (`*` = required):

```json
{
  "title": "Team Oreo Wins the Championship",
  "excerpt": "A recap of the biggest match.",
  "content": "<h2>Match day</h2><p>Full story…</p>",
  "category": "News",
  "author": "Oreo Admin",
  "featuredImage": {
    "url": "https://…",
    "alt": "…"
  },
  "status": "published"
}
```

- `title`* — 3–200 chars.
- `excerpt`* — 10–500 chars.
- `content`* — HTML, sanitized server-side.
- `category`* — required.
- `author`* — required.
- `featuredImage.url`* — required.
- `status` — optional; defaults to `draft`.

**Publishing rules:**

- `status: "published"` sets `publishedAt` on first publish only; `status: "draft"` resets it to `null`.
- Slug is editable via `PATCH { "slug": "…" }` — collisions auto-suffix `-2`, `-3`…
- Every admin route returns `401` cleanly without a valid session (verified, not assumed).

### 🖼️ Image Uploads

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Contract |
|---|---|---|---|
| 🔵 POST | `/api/admin/uploads` | Admin | `multipart/form-data`, field name `image` · JPEG/PNG/WebP · ≤ 5 MB |

**Example response — `201`:**

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/…",
    "publicId": "team-oreo/blogs/…",
    "bytes": 102400
  },
  "message": "Image uploaded"
}
```

Use `data.url` as `featuredImage.url`.

Wrong type → `400 INVALID_FILE` · Over 5 MB → `413 FILE_TOO_LARGE`.

